<title>EGYPT: Egypt tourism revenues slip slightly in April.</title>
<headline>Egypt tourism revenues slip slightly in April.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt earned $326 million from its tourism industry in April, slightly lower than the $329 million it received in the previous month, official figures made available on Tuesday showed.</p>
<p>Tourism is one of Egypt's main foreign currency earners. In April 1996, Egypt earned $290 million from the industry.</p>
<p>The figures showed 344,000 tourists visited Egypt in April, slightly less than the 354,000 who came in March. The April visitors spent 2.389 million nights compared to 2.408 million nights in March.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290 mf ceh</p>
</text>
